cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "POCSAG RF Message Injection — Proof of Concept"
message: "If you reference this educational research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Akshit"
    alias: "Akshit0203"
abstract: >-
  A controlled, educational reconstruction of the unauthenticated,
  unencrypted message-injection weakness in the legacy POCSAG paging
  protocol, demonstrated with commodity SDR hardware (HackRF One +
  PortaPack H2+ running Mayhem, and Flipper Zero running RogueMaster).
  Published to inform defenders and regulators about the risk of
  trusting broadcast paging for safety-critical communications.
keywords:
  - POCSAG
  - SDR
  - RF security
  - SIGINT
  - wireless protocol analysis
  - critical infrastructure
  - HackRF
  - Flipper Zero
license: MIT
date-released: 2025-05-13
